-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Oct 27 06:31:10 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.20.0:
  * Add MXFP6 (E2M3) quantization with mxfp6-pack-quantized format,
    and a MXFP4xFP8 quantization scheme
  * Add layerwise compression and decompression, and an expert
    sparsity config for MoE models
  * Add FP8 block dequantizer from_pretrained and fuse the quantize
    and FP4-pack Triton kernels
  * Offload: support device_map="disk", reuse safetensors handles
    via disk_load_context, group subgraph staging reads, and batch
    metadata exchange in distributed dispatch; fix onloading of
    offloaded children in set_onload_device
  * convert_checkpoint gains max_workers="auto" by default and
    quieter file-copying logs; support MTP checkpoint export
  * Quantization fixes: NVFP4 on A100, 4-bit unpack by splitting
    bytes (also on big-endian hosts), contiguous packed INT
    tensors, qparam init on disk, weight transforms and
    dense-saving of quantized Linear/Embedding subclasses,
    router bias pruning fix
  * Parse CT_ENFORCE_EAGER as a boolean, so =0/=false disables it;
    skip default-valued fields in QuantizationArgs serialization
  * Drop Python 3.10: minimum is now 3.11
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Sep 26 20:52:00 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.19.0:
  * BREAKING: GPTQ group/dynamic activation ordering has been removed.
    actorder='group'/'dynamic' and actorder=True now raise a ValueError
    instead of warning; use actorder='weight' instead
  * Checkpoint conversion can now be scheduled across multiple GPUs by
    measured free memory, using a profiler-based memory estimator
  * Add a MagnitudeExpertPruner converter that structurally prunes MoE
    experts by magnitude, and allow chaining converters in one pipeline
  * Support decompressing models under distributed execution; fix dtype
    mismatch and tensor shapes in the distributed offload caches, which
    broke tied and multimodal models
  * Fix an AttributeError in QuantizedKVCache for transformers 5 models
    that read the KV cache structurally during calibration
  * Observer resolution and defaulting moved to llm-compressor;
    automatic qstrategy inference has been removed
  * Faster model-free PTQ on meta tensors and a memoized calculate_range;
    fix Triton cast_to_fp4 rounding for fp32/fp16 near FP4 boundaries
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes for
    the full list

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Aug 12 05:22:58 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.18.0:
  * Add QuantizationConfig.merge and TransformConfig.merge, allowing
    compression of models that already carry a quantization config
  * Only apply quantization schemes to Linear, Embedding and Attention
    layers, and ignore non-linear MoE gate layers
  * Add a Triton implementation of cast_to_fp4 and make FP4 packing
    faster and less memory hungry
  * Fix NVFP4 packing for float32 inputs
  * Fix KV cache quantization for composite multimodal models
  * Several offloading fixes: force offloading of buffers, fix disk
    distributed module compression, fix tied transform weight
    detection for offloaded models
  * Fix MTP tensor copy from indexed checkpoints
  * Validate block structure dimensions and length
  * Deprecate actorder group
- Add Requires on python-psutil, newly required by upstream

-------------------------------------------------------------------
